# Playground

The playground block renders an editable Carve source pane, a rendered pane, an HTML pane, and an AST pane.

::: note "Browser payload"
The playground ships the Carve engine to the browser. CarvePress only copies those assets when a rendered page contains a playground block.
:::

::: playground
```carve
# Try Carve

/italic/, *bold*, _underline_, ~strike~, =highlight=.

::: details "Disclosure"
Edit the source and the preview updates.
:::
```
:::

Use the static `::: compare` block from [Carve Syntax](/guide/carve-syntax) when a page only needs a fixed source and output demonstration.
